      "value": "@{59b1485b4493c77bec9117bd|full_name}: Thank you for the reply, but Im not sure if its that, I have another Avatar that has more stuff on it, and is quite bigger and that one isnt banned.  Regardless neither do the 80mb to 2gb thing, all the textures too are 2k with a bunch of them being 512 to 1k. If this is really performance related due to the amount of outfits n textures(which would be weird since the other isnt 'banned'\" ) wouldnt it be better to put something other than 'security checks failed' on it? And since when is regular avatar size getting punished? I thought thats what download size filter is for, I feel thats a bit harsh to do to avatars that are only used around friends in private, when the default download size limit should filter them out.",
